# Methylation k-mer browser tracks

`scripts/generate_methylation_kmer_tracks.py` reads the labeled token rows in
paired retrained and pretrained prediction files without aggregating them into
5.4 kb windows. The validated browser interval for the current tokenizer is
`[genomic_position, genomic_position + 6)`.

## Scores and categorical states

Correctness delta is retrained correctness minus baseline correctness:

- `+1`: rescued — retrained correct, baseline wrong.
- `-1`: harmed — retrained wrong, baseline correct.
- `0`: both correct or both wrong; categorical BED tracks keep these distinct.

`true_probability_delta` is the retrained probability assigned to the observed
class minus the pretrained probability assigned to that class. It is not
computed for the atlas (mean-label) baseline because that cache contains a
class, not class probabilities.

Tissue bedGraph values average participant results at the exact k-mer coordinate.
The summary retains rescued, harmed, both-correct, and both-wrong participant
counts, standard errors, label counts, and coverage.

## Generate tracks

Priority high-variability groups for all discovered test results:

```bash
python3 scripts/generate_methylation_kmer_tracks.py \
  --results-root scripts/results/downsampled_standard_ratio_0p25_lr_3e-05 \
  --output-dir scripts/results/methylation_kmer_tracks
```

A small participant/chromosome run that also writes categorical participant
tracks:

```bash
python3 scripts/generate_methylation_kmer_tracks.py \
  --results-root scripts/results/downsampled_standard_ratio_0p25_lr_3e-05 \
  --output-dir scripts/results/methylation_kmer_tracks_Z0000044P_chr21 \
  --participant Z0000044P --chrom chr21 --participant-tracks
```

An atlas-versus-retraining-only pilot with unambiguous track and item names:

```bash
python3 scripts/generate_methylation_kmer_tracks.py \
  --results-root scripts/results/downsampled_standard_ratio_0p25_lr_3e-05 \
  --output-dir scripts/results/methylation_kmer_tracks_Z0000044P_chr21_retrained_vs_atlas \
  --participant Z0000044P --chrom chr21 --participant-tracks --baseline atlas
```

This writes `retrained_vs_atlas` tracks whose participant item names contain
`atlas=<class>` and `retrain=<class>`.

A tissue-level atlas comparison aggregates paired participant outcomes at each
exact k-mer and can require a minimum participant count:

```bash
python3 scripts/generate_methylation_kmer_tracks.py \
  --results-root scripts/results/downsampled_standard_ratio_0p25_lr_3e-05 \
  --output-dir analysis/Heart-Cardiomyocyte_chr21_retrained_vs_atlas \
  --tissue Heart-Cardiomyocyte --chrom chr21 --baseline atlas \
  --min-participants-per-kmer 3
```

The complete aggregate remains in `kmer_summary.tsv.gz`.
`browser_kmer_summary.tsv.gz` and the browser tracks contain only rows meeting
the coverage threshold.

To emit each tissue separately and a second aggregation across every selected
sample, add `--combined-samples-track` and omit the tissue filter:

```bash
python3 scripts/generate_methylation_kmer_tracks.py \
  --results-root scripts/results/downsampled_standard_ratio_0p25_lr_3e-05 \
  --output-dir analysis/all_tissues_and_combined_chr21 \
  --chrom chr21 --baseline atlas --combined-samples-track \
  --min-participants-per-kmer 3
```

The combined track is named `All-samples`. Each sample is compared with its
own tissue atlas before correctness changes are pooled, so tissues with more
samples contribute proportionally more observations.

Filters `--tissue`, `--participant`, `--chrom`, `--bin-group`, and `--baseline`
may be repeated. Baseline choices are `pretrained` and `atlas`; by default all
available baselines are included. The default views are `bin1`, `bin2`, `bin3`,
`bin4`, `bin5`, `bins3-5`, and `bins4-5`. Bins 1 and 2 are standalone
views and are not added to either combined-bin view. Generation refuses to
overwrite a non-empty output directory.

## Outputs

- `tracks/*.correctness_delta.bedGraph`: mean correctness change at each k-mer.
- `tracks/*.true_probability_delta.bedGraph`: mean true-class probability change.
- `tracks/*.status.bed`: BED9 tissue records with compact `n#_r#_h#` names,
  where `n` is contributing participants, `r` is rescued, and `h` is harmed.
  The complete both-correct and both-wrong counts remain in the summary tables.
- `participant_tracks/*.status.bed`: exact rescued/harmed/both-correct/both-wrong
  records when `--participant-tracks` is requested.
- `kmer_summary.tsv.gz`: complete tissue/k-mer audit before coverage filtering.
- `browser_kmer_summary.tsv.gz`: the rows shown in tissue browser tracks after
  applying `--min-participants-per-kmer`.
- `participant_kmer_summary.tsv.gz`: participant rows when requested.
- `qc_summary.tsv`: variability coverage.
- `selected_manifest.tsv`: exact prediction paths and checkpoint selection.
- `igv_session.xml` and `ucsc_custom_tracks.txt`: complete browser bundles.
- `ucsc_categorical_tracks.txt`: categorical-only UCSC upload without numerical
  bedGraphs. With `--participant-tracks`, it contains the exact participant
  categories: green rescued, red harmed, blue both-correct, and gray both-wrong.
  Otherwise it contains the tissue aggregate status BEDs.

For large multi-tissue output, IGV and individual tracks are preferable to the
self-contained UCSC text bundle. bigWig/bigBed conversion tools are not installed
in the current environment, so this first implementation emits standard sorted
BED and bedGraph files.

## Real pilot

The checked pilot at
`scripts/results/methylation_kmer_tracks_Z0000044P_chr21` contains participant
Z0000044P, Heart-Cardiomyocyte, chr21. It validates 54,509 paired k-mers and
matches 51,838 (95.1%) to variability data. Open its `igv_session.xml` with
hg38, or upload its `ucsc_custom_tracks.txt`.

Coordinates inherit the source hg38 and 0-based convention used by the prediction
windows. The 5.4 kb `window_id` is retained only for pairing and context, not as
the reported result interval.
